          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em free abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[S]
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            whose elements are
            %em
              formal
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
            of elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#Definition Definition
          #FreeAbelianGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \colon Ab \longrightarrow Set
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              from the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of abelian groups, to the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              of sets. This has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free construction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Ab
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}[-] \colon Set \longrightarrow Ab
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is the
              = succeed "." do
                %em free abelian group functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %strong free abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[S] \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free object
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with respect to this
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
          %p
            Of course, this notion is meant to be invariant under isomorphism: it doesn’t depend on the left adjoint chosen. Thus, if a functor of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom_{Set}(S, U-): Ab \to Set
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            by an abelian group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a free abelian group on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom_{Ab}(A, -) \cong \hom_{Set}(S, U-)
          %p
            corresponds, via the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to U A
            which exhibits
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is so equipped with such a universal arrow
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to U A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            “the” free abelian group on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Explicit descriptions of free abelian groups are discussed
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Properties"} below
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#in_terms_of_formal_linear_combinations In terms of formal linear combinations
          #FormalLinearCombination.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong formal linear combination
              of elements of a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a : S \to \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              such that only finitely many of the values
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_s \in \mathbb{Z}
              are non-zero.
            %p
              Identifying an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
              with the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to \mathbb{Z}
              which sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathbb{Z}
              and all other elements to 0, this is written as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi s
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi s
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a = \sum_{s \in S} a_s \cdot s
                    \\,.
            %p
              In this expression one calls
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_s \in \mathbb{Z}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              in the formal linear combination.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalLinearCombination"}
              of formal linear combinations makes sense with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A[S] \coloneqq \mathbb{Z}[S] \otimes A
                    \\,.
          #GroupOfFormalLinearCombinations.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %strong group of formal linear combinations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[S]
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              whose underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              is that of formal linear combinations, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalLinearCombination"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi s
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi s
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi s
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi s
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\sum_{s \in S} a_s \cdot s)
                    +
                    (\sum_{s \in S} b_s \cdot s)
                    \=
                    \\sum_{s \in S} (a_s + b_s) \cdot s
                    \\,.
          #FreeAbelianGroupIsGroupOfFormalLinearCombinations.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The free abelian group on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              is, up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combinations"} formal linear combinations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupOfFormalLinearCombinations"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .num_defn
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a set, the free abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[S]
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              = succeed "-copies" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|S|}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              with itself:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}[S] \simeq \oplus_{s \in S} \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          %p
          #FreeAbelianGroupFunctorSendsProductsToTensorProducts.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The free abelian group of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times Z
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S, T \,\in\, Sets
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of
              the free abelian groups of the factors:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}[S \times T]
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{Z}[S] \otimes \mathbb{Z}[T]
                    \\,.
            %p
              In other words, as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}[-]
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Set \longrightarrow Ab
            %p
              this is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
          This follows, for instance, from the above expression (Prop.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeAbelianGroupIsGroupOfFormalLinearCombinations"}
          %p
          #FreeSimplicialAbelianGroupConstrIsStrongMonoidal.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_\bullet
              which is (or is
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly equivalent to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              — because the resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              (under the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
              of that space. But since
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+simplicial+sets"} product of simplicial sets
                  is degreewise that in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a{:href => "monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence#MonoidalCategoryStructures"} tensor product of simplicial abelian groups
                  is degreewise the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
            %p
              the above Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeAbelianGroupFunctorSendsProductsToTensorProducts"}
              implies that also the functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi sAb
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}[-]
                    \\;\colon\;
                    sSet \longrightarrow sAb
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sAb"} sAb
